  "title": "Counting under branched twists is #P-hard: the boundary is two-sided on the knot's graphs",
  "subject": "The complexity of counting colourings of the knot's incidence graphs under sign classes other than the knot's own",
  "conclusion": "Counting colourings of cubic bipartite Pfaffian graphs under signings is #P-hard, by reduction from NAE-3SAT counting through merge paths, dead caps and the sharpened soft crossing, and the instances are twisted on all three branches at every junction. Since the knot's own class and every unbranched twist count in polynomial time, the knot's sign class and the branching of twists away from it divide easy from hard.",
